.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH AUTH-SERVICE 1
.SH NAME
auth\-service \- authorize & authenticate members
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBauth\-service\fR [FLAGS] [OPTIONS] path
.SH DESCRIPTION
A command\-line service for managing authenticated members.
.SH FLAGS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose logging.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR=\fIoutput\fR [default: \fIstdout\fR]
The output destination.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBPORT\fR [default: \fI3000\fR]
The network port to listen to.
.SH "usage note"
The service should be started before requests arrive.


Use the environment variable to select its port.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
Successful program execution.
.TP
\fB1\fR
Unsuccessful program execution.
.TP
\fB101\fR
The program panicked.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
run the service
\fB$ auth\-service \-\-verbose\fR
.br
now listening
.SH AUTHORS
.P
.RS 2
.nf
Alice Person <alice@example.com>
Bob Human
